# Build context for the API image (see Dockerfile, docs/DEPLOY.md).
#
# Without this file the context was 1.3 GB - node_modules alone is 1.1 GB - and every build
# uploaded all of it before running a single instruction. The image only needs the Python
# workspace, the small research data files the pipelines read, and the bundle manifests.

# The console is a separate Vercel deployment; none of it belongs in the API image.
apps/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Version control and local Python environments.
.git/
.github/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Generated at runtime into the mounted volume, never baked into the image: the entrypoint
# builds the city on first boot and runs write into data/.
city/
data/
docs/screens/

# Evidence screenshots and raw captures - 19 MB of the 21 MB in docs/. The pipelines read the
# curated files beside them (hotspots_*.geojson, ground_truth_*.geojson, bmc_aws_stations.json,
# data_sources.md), which are kilobytes and must stay.
docs/research/_raw/
docs/*.pdf

# Local tooling and secrets.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.vercel/
*.log

# The Rust routing service's build output (P8.12): 167 MB that the image never runs, since
# the API serves the Python router. The crate's source is small and stays.
services/route-rs/target/
